ed to have 48 children ages 4-10 years old in one group for over 30 minutes exceeding the maximum group size allowed.  The children were seperated into two groups during the inspection.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026486769","violation_type_title":"Exceeding Maximum Group Size - 3 and 4 Years (30 mins) (26 TAC §744.1609(a)(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221117-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-744-1203-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221117","date":"2022-11-17","original_code":"744.1203(5)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-12-02","finding":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Children in Control: It was observed that children in the care of 2 caregivers were out of control.  Children were observed running with stick candy in their mouths, climbing on tables, throwing liquid soap and various other objects at each other, pushing and hitting  one another, playing in water fountains, and jumping from the cafeteria stage without proper redirection.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026246222","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Children in Control (26 TAC §744.1203(5))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221117-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-744-1203-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221117","date":"2022-11-17","original_code":"744.1203(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-12-02","finding":"Responsibilities of Caregivers- Supervision of Children: It was observed that 48 children in care were not being adequately supervised by two caregivers.  Children were observed hiding out of sight, running in unsupervised hallways, plugging in cell phone chargers, using personal cell phones without content supervision and crawling into an unsupervised kitchen area.  Caregivers were asked to regain control before licensing left the operation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026406988","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Caregivers- Supervision of Children (26 TAC §744.1203(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221018","date":"2022-10-18","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":2,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905860329","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905860329","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2022-10-18","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221018-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-744-605-16","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221018","date":"2022-10-18","original_code":"744.605(16)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-11-09","finding":"Required Admission Information-Food Allergy Emergency Plan: There was one child file indicating a food allergy and there was no emergency allergy plan to review.  The director indicated that there were more children enrolled with peanut allergies but there was no documentation available for review.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026446789","violation_type_title":"Required Admission Information-Food Allergy Emergency Plan (26 TAC §744.605(16))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221018-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-744-401-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1411609-i20221018","date":"2022-10-18","original_code":"744.401(4)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-11-09","finding":"Posting Requirements-Emergency Evacuation and Relocation Diagram: There was no emergency relocation/ evacuation information available for review at the operation.","t